content:
A Plus guarantee claim on Northgate Memberships that the primary member confirms settles one completed membership year, the reward year of the most recent year-end Annual Reward conversion on the membership; the refund is booked against the fee charge that paid the Plus premium for that year and returned to that charge's tender, and the membership moves to its base tier the same day.

The primary member may claim the guarantee for a completed membership year only where that year shows a guarantee shortfall, and the amount the claim pays is the guarantee refund rather than the plain difference between the Plus premium and the year's Annual Reward.

## What the confirmation records

Confirming the claim is the primary member's own action. One confirmation:

- marks the member's recorded guarantee claim request as confirmed;
- books the guarantee refund on the membership ledger against the stated fee charge for the stated membership year, returned to the stated tender;
- moves the membership to the stated base tier from that day.

Afterwards the claim shows as confirmed, the refund appears on the ledger and the membership carries the base tier.

## Invocation

The tool is `confirm_plus_guarantee_claim_e9c317f9`. It belongs to the member: member services unlocks it and hands it over, and the customer themselves runs it to confirm their own claim.

## Parameters

| Parameter | Meaning | Format |
|---|---|---|
| `membership_request_id` | the reference number of the member's guarantee claim request, as returned by the membership request lookup and read out to the member | identifier |
| `membership_id` | the membership reference number the claim is on, as returned by the membership lookup | identifier |
| `source_txn_id` | the reference number of the fee charge the refund is booked against, as returned by the membership ledger lookup | identifier |
| `term_end_date` | the last day of the completed membership year the claim settles | calendar date YYYY-MM-DD, local club date, never empty |
| `guarantee_refund` | the guarantee refund paid | USD with 2 decimal places, always positive; stored rounded half up to 2 decimal places as passed |
| `tender` | where the refund is returned | one of the tender codes below |
| `downgrade_tier` | the official tier the membership moves to | one of the tier names below, exactly |

`tender` takes exactly one of:
  - `cash_or_debit` — back to the debit card or as cash when the charge was paid that way;
  - `northgate_visa` — back to the member's Northgate Rewards Visa card;
  - `northgate_store_card` — back to the member's Northgate Store Card;
  - `other_credit_card` — back to the other credit card the charge was paid with;
  - `shop_card` — onto a Northgate Shop Card;
  - `reward_certificate` — never used for a refund destination, only for charges paid with a certificate;
  - `not_applicable` — never used for a refund, only for entries that carry no payment.

`downgrade_tier` takes exactly one of:

  - Northgate Student Club Membership — the discounted student tier;
  - Northgate Heroes Club Membership — the discounted military and first-responder tier;
  - Northgate Club Membership — the consumer base tier a Northgate Club Plus Membership moves to;
  - Northgate Business Membership — the business base tier a Northgate Business Plus Membership moves to;
  - Northgate Club Plus Membership — the consumer Plus tier;
  - Northgate Business Plus Membership — the business Plus tier.

## Return

A text receipt reading "Guarantee claim confirmed", followed by the refund entry reference on the membership ledger, the claim request reference, the refund amount in USD with 2 decimals, the tender, the membership year end (YYYY-MM-DD) and the tier now held. A receipt starting "Guarantee claim confirmed" means the claim, the refund and the tier change are all recorded.
